From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Settings: no settings for what the device cannot do

Settings showed on PW3 (walked page by page, Test V37) entries that can have no
effect there. Each is now shown by a condition the device answers, as AOSP
already does for some (KEYCODE_POWER for "power button ends call", rotation
support for "lock screen rotation"):
  * Wi-Fi Direct: FEATURE_WIFI_DIRECT (PW3's driver runs station mode only);
  * network rating provider: a valid network scorer is installed;
  * WPS push button and PIN: not shown. WPS is insecure and deprecated by the
    Wi-Fi Alliance; Android 9 removed it;
  * premium SMS access: the device can send SMS (TelephonyManager.isSmsCapable);
  * default notification, alarm and ring tones, mono audio, screen readers and
    text-to-speech output: FEATURE_AUDIO_OUTPUT (PW3 has no speaker);
  * large mouse pointer, click after the pointer stops, pointer speed, physical
    keyboard: such a device is connected, or can be (USB host or Bluetooth);
  * accessibility shortcut (both volume keys held): the device has volume keys;
  * trust agents: an app provides one;
  * encrypt tablet: StorageManager.isEncryptable() (PW3: ro.crypto.state is
    "unsupported"; vold cannot encrypt its data);
  * backup: FEATURE_BACKUP (without it the backup service does not run);
  * assist and voice input: an app can be the assistant (the picker would
    offer only "None"); it appears when one is installed;
  * serial number: not when it is unknown.
The network page's data usage summary counted mobile data only, "0 B used" on
a device that has none: there it counts Wi-Fi. Captions stay: without audio
they are how a video in the browser can be followed.

